{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality"],"declarations":34,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.level3_no_fixed_point_level4_has_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.level3_no_fixed_point_level4_has_one","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L235-L243","doc":"**The level-3 / level-4 asymmetry, in one statement.** The pair (`n = 2`) has\nno charge-conjugation-invariant block; the first shell (`n = 4`) has one. The\ncorpus's architectural claim is therefore a theorem about partitions, not a\nmodelling choice — and it is also the reason the pair layer cannot inherit\ncharge symmetry from the shell: there is no invariant block at the pair for the\nshell's invariant one to restrict to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.selfDual4_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.selfDual4_iff","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L229-L233","doc":"**And it is the only one.** So the shell has exactly one charge-conjugation\nfixed point where the pair has none. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.p22_selfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.p22_selfDual","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L226-L227","doc":"**At `n = 4` the block `(2,2)` IS self-dual** — the level-4 half. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.shellDuality4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.shellDuality4","kind":"def","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L220-L224","doc":"The `n = 4` instance of the same carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.conj4_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.conj4_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L217-L218","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.conj4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.conj4","kind":"def","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L208-L215","doc":"The transpose on partitions of 4: `(4)* = (1,1,1,1)`, `(3,1)* = (2,1,1)`,\nand `(2,2)* = (2,2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.instDecidableEqBlock4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.instDecidableEqBlock4","kind":"instance","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L206-L206","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block4.p1111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block4.p1111","kind":"ctor","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L205-L205","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block4.p211","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block4.p211","kind":"ctor","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L204-L204","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block4.p22","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block4.p22","kind":"ctor","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L203-L203","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block4.p31","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block4.p31","kind":"ctor","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L202-L202","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block4.p4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block4.p4","kind":"ctor","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L201-L201","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block4","kind":"inductive","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L199-L206","doc":"The five partitions of 4, the Wedderburn blocks of `H₄(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.conj_fixed_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.conj_fixed_iff","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L185-L187","doc":"`C` fixes the `pp` factor iff `2z = h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.charge_symmetric_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.charge_symmetric_iff","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L176-L183","doc":"**The pair layer is charge-symmetric iff `h = 0`.** `f_pp = z` and\n`f_nn = z - h` agree exactly when the deformation parameter vanishes, i.e. when\n`q = q⁻¹`. The framework buys its `q`-deformation and its charge asymmetry with\nthe same parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.trace_heckeConj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.trace_heckeConj","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L172-L174","doc":"`tr (C σ) = h - z`. With `f_nn = z - h` this says **`C(f_pp) = -f_nn`** —\nthe charge conjugate of the `pp` factor is *minus* the `nn` factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.eigen_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.eigen_swap","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L160-L166","doc":"**The eigenvalue exchange.** On the one-dimensional blocks `σ` acts by `q`\nand by `-q⁻¹`; writing `h = q - q⁻¹`, the swap sends the first to the second and\nback. Stated as the two `h`-identities so that `q⁻¹` need only appear as a named\nelement `qi`, never as an inverse the ring has to supply. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.heckeConj_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.heckeConj_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L155-L158","doc":"The swap is an involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.heckeConj_isHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.heckeConj_isHecke","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L148-L153","doc":"**The swap preserves the Hecke relation** — so it really is an automorphism\nof the algebra and not merely a relabelling of eigenvalues. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.heckeConj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.heckeConj","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L145-L146","doc":"The block swap on the generator: `C σ = h - σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.IsHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.IsHecke","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L142-L143","doc":"The `H₂` relation in inverse-free form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.no_conj_invariant_separating_label","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.no_conj_invariant_separating_label","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L128-L135","doc":"**The `qou-rvse` assignment cannot exist.** No `C`-invariant isospin label\ngives the two blocks different values — so none assigns `(2)` the triplet and\n`(1,1)` the singlet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.isospin_const_of_conj_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.isospin_const_of_conj_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L120-L126","doc":"**A `C`-invariant labelling of the blocks is constant.** Stated for an\narbitrary target so it applies to `T` valued in `ℕ`, `ℚ`, or anything else. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.no_selfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.no_selfDual","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L108-L113","doc":"**At `n = 2` no block is self-dual.** The carrier defines a self-dual shell\nas a fixed point of the transpose (`selfDual_iff_fixed`), and at `n = 2` the\ntranspose has none. This is the sharp form of the interpretation block's claim\nthat Schur–Weyl self-duality is *exact at level 4* but broken at level 3: the\npair simply has no self-conjugate partition to carry it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.shellDuality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.shellDuality","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L100-L106","doc":"The `n = 2` instance of the corpus's **own** Schur–Weyl self-duality carrier\n(`QOU.BraidKnot.ShellSchurWeylSelfDuality`), so that what follows is a statement\ninside that structure rather than a parallel construction beside it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.conj_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.conj_ne","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L94-L98","doc":"`C` has no fixed block. This is the sharp form of \"the swap is not the\nidentity\": there is nowhere for a `C`-eigenlabel to sit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.conj_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.conj_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L90-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.conj_alt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.conj_alt","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.conj_sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.conj_sym","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.conj","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L80-L85","doc":"Charge conjugation on blocks: `λ ↦ λ*`. At `n = 2` the conjugate of `(2)` is\n`(1,1)`, so `C` is the **swap** — this is `shell-schur-weyl-self-duality-proof`\nstep 4 evaluated at `n = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.instDecidableEqBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.instDecidableEqBlock","kind":"instance","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block.alt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block.alt","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block.sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block.sym","kind":"ctor","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairIsospinAssignment.Block","kind":"inductive","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairIsospinAssignment.lean#L74-L78","doc":"The two Wedderburn blocks of `H₂(q)`, indexed by the partitions of 2. ","signatureChunk":0}]}